implementationPlan.description:
Final step: load adversarial-self-review and read this task's diff as an attacker.
(1) Mutation check in a scratch copy, never in the checkout. Copy only the files the test reads and run with NODE_PATH=<checkout>/moe-vscode/node_modules (mem:convention-vscode-port-mutant-checkref). Each of these mutants must fail an agent-seats row by assertion, not by a harness error:
- drop the onLaunched call;
- call it after sendText;
- let a throwing onLaunched abort the launch;
- drop the WORKER_DEREGISTERED case;
- drop the workerId type guard;
- skip _onWorkerDeregistered.dispose();
- send reason 'closed';
- remove onLaunched from one launch site;
- move wireAgentSeats below the autoConnect block.
(2) Activation order: survivors are marked launched before wireAgentSeats subscribes and before connect, so the first resendGone never deregisters a live seat.
(3) A seat launched and closed before its processId resolves: closed() still deregisters it, because it was mapped synchronously. Its pid is recorded afterwards and pruned by the save after the ack.
(4) A reconnected terminal that mapSurvivor mapped and that then closes is deregistered exactly once.
(5) With VS Code's persistent sessions off, a reload kills the shells, so isProcessAlive is false and the old seats are resent, as in JetBrains.
(6) No new import in MoeDaemonClient.ts or AgentLauncher.ts; no existing test file changed; createTerminal options, terminal names and commands are byte-identical.
Fix real defects inside the three source files or the new test. If anything changed, re-run checkRef 1. Record the findings in the step note.
